description:
Growe welcomes those who are excited to:

•
Lead and develop the Customer Support function within a fast-growing iGaming environment;

•
Scale a high-performing VIP Customer Support team aligned with the company’s growth and operational goals;

•
Define and drive key performance metrics, including CSAT, FRT, SLA, Quality, AHT, FCR and productivity;

•
Maintain a consistently high standard of communication and service quality across all customer interactions;

•
Establish clear processes, workflows and escalation standards to ensure efficient and scalable Support operations;

•
Analyse operational and customer data and turn insights into actionable improvements;

•
Work closely with QA and Training teams to continuously improve agent performance, knowledge and communication standards;

•
Identify opportunities for automation, self-service and process optimisation to improve efficiency and player experience;

•
Act as the voice of the customer by identifying recurring pain points and working with Product and Operations teams to address them;

•
Collaborate closely with CRM and Account Management/VIP teams.

We need your professional experience:

•
5+ years of experience in Customer Support or similar customer-facing roles;

•
1+ year of experience in a Team Lead, Team Manager, or similar leadership position;

•
Strong analytical mindset and ability to use operational and customer data to drive improvements;

•
Experience working with customer support performance metrics such as CSAT, FRT, SLA, Quality, AHT, FCR and productivity;

•
Experience working with Product, Operations, CRM or Account Management/VIP teams will be a plus;

•
Experience in iGaming, with understanding of the player journey and industry-specific customer needs will be a plus;

•
Upper-Intermediate English level (written and spoken) for daily communication within an international team.

We appreciate if you have those personal features:

•
Strong communication skills: communicate clearly and effectively with team members, provide constructive feedback, maintain high communication standards within the team and build strong relationships with cross-functional stakeholders;

•
Leadership and people-management mindset: motivate and support the team, create a positive working environment, develop team members and confidently manage performance and challenging situations;

•
Customer-oriented mindset: genuinely understand customer needs, stay focused on delivering a high-quality player experience and proactively identify opportunities to improve the customer journey;

•
Analytical and problem-solving mindset: identify the root causes of operational and customer-related issues, make data-driven decisions and turn insights into practical improvements for the team and Support function.

We are seeking those who align with our core values:

•
GROWE TOGETHER: Our team is our main asset. We work together and support each other to achieve our common goals;

•
DRIVE RESULT OVER PROCESS: We set ambitious, clear, measurable goals in line with our strategy and driving Growe to success;

•
BE READY FOR CHANGE: We see challenges as opportunities to grow and evolve. We adapt today to win tomorrow.

Senior People Business Partner

Location : London&nbsp;
Office requirement : Minimum 2 days in the office

Employment type : Permanent&nbsp;

As our Senior People Business Partner you’ll:

Report to the VP, People and Culture, and partner closely with our Chief Revenue Officer, Chief Marketing Officer and their senior leaders to own the talent agenda for our Go-To-Market (GTM) teams, translating the business and People &amp; Culture (P&amp;C) strategy into an impactful plan that drives business growth, high performance, engagement and inclusion.&nbsp;

You’ll:

• Develop a deep understanding of Revenue and Marketing, collaborating with your business leaders to translate commercial strategy (growth targets, territory changes, GTM shifts) into people plans that deliver growth, efficiency, engagement and inclusion.&nbsp;

• Use internal and external data insights to proactively identify strategic and operational opportunities and address challenges, connecting the dots and influencing key business and talent decisions relating to org design and talent management (including performance, reward, recognition and growth).&nbsp;

• Provide consultation and coaching for leaders and managers on performance, talent development and employee relations, aligning to the GWI approach.

• Support compensation design specific to sales roles (OTE structures, commission plans, territory/quota-linked incentives) in partnership with Finance.

• Champion culture and engagement initiatives adapted to the realities of a target-driven environment.

• Drive performance managem

